	"burn.title": "Maximum push",
	"burn.duration": "Duration",
	"burn.desc": "Normally the team slows itself down to make the budget last: it stops once it has spent the day's share, stays quiet outside working hours and eases off as the window fills up. This switch suspends those brakes for a single window, when you need the team to push right now.",
	"burn.desc_measured": "It does not promise to spend everything: on the night this feature was born, with every override in place, usage stopped between 6% and 19% of the window. Finding openings and analysing them mostly waits on the network, not on the model, and removing the pauses does not change that. It exists so the team obeys when you ask.",
	"burn.state_off": "off — the team paces itself to make the budget last",
	"burn.state_active": "on — expires in %s",
	"burn.state_soon": "on — expires in %s, then pacing returns by itself",
	"burn.state_unknown": "state unreadable — the team did not answer",
	"burn.state_unsupported": "unavailable — the team container is older than the game",
	"burn.left_h": "%s h",
	"burn.left_hm": "%s h %s min",
	"burn.left_m": "%s min",
	"burn.left_soon": "less than a minute",
	"burn.sending": "sending to the team…",
	"burn.failed": "failed — %s",
	"burn.confirm_title": "Turn on maximum push?",
	"burn.confirm_body": "The team stops slowing itself down to make the budget last: no daily stop, no off-hours pause, no reduced pace as the window fills up.\n\n• It switches itself off after %s hours — the ceiling is %s: there is no permanent form, and it never stays on by forgetfulness.\n\n• Four brakes do not yield anyway: %s. These are not savings — past the weekly limit the provider stops answering, and past the memory ceiling the machine slows everything down. Forcing them would produce less work, not more.\n\n• Oversight moves to the Coordinator: without the automatic brakes it is up to them to stop an agent that burns without producing. You can revoke at any time from the same switch.",
	"burn.confirm_ok": "Turn on for %s hours",

